lagfinder.tip.sort=Sorting\nAverage: what costs the most over the whole scan.\nPeak: the worst single tick - finds things that lag hard but rarely.\nSpikes: how often it went over the spike threshold.
lagfinder.tip.avg=Average time per tick\nTime spent over the whole scan divided by the ticks measured.
lagfinder.tip.peak=Peak\nThe longest it took in one single tick (or frame) of the scan.
lagfinder.tip.avg_fps=FPS cost\nHow much higher FPS would be without it. The bigger the number, the more it lags.
lagfinder.tip.peak_fps=Worst drop\nHow far FPS fell in the frame where this took the longest. A big number means stutters.
lagfinder.tip.share=Share\nPart of an average tick (or frame) this takes.
lagfinder.tip.spikes=Spikes\nTicks (or frames) in which it alone took longer than the spike threshold.
lagfinder.tip.calls=Calls\nHow many times it ran per tick (or frame), on average.
lagfinder.tip.active=Active\nPart of the ticks (or frames) in which it ran at all.
lagfinder.tip.instances=Instances\nHow many of them were seen during the scan.
