lagfinder.alloc.hint=Pick a line to see it here and on the graph. A click opens it: type → classes → methods.
lagfinder.alloc.hint2=Tab switches between types and classes. Pick a mod on the left to see only what its classes create.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_sort=Sorting
By size: the bytes allocated, the most first.
By name: alphabetical.
By mod: grouped by the mod of the type or class.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_threads=Only the scanned thread (%s), or every thread of the game: chunk loading, networking, rendering...
lagfinder.tip.alloc_threads_off=Without the Flight Recorder only the scanned thread (%s) is seen.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_by_type=Every type of objects created (int[], String, NBTTagCompound...), with the classes creating it under it, and their methods and lines under those.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_no_types=This Java has no Flight Recorder (Java 16 or later is needed): the types of the objects are not known.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_by_creator=Every class creating objects (the nearest one that isn't Java's or a library's), with the types it creates under it, and its methods and lines under those.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_all_mods=All the objects created, by the classes of every mod.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_pick_mod=Click to see only what this mod's classes create.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_jfr=Java's Flight Recorder took samples of the objects created, each with its type and where it was created; each stands for the bytes allocated since the one before, so the bytes add up to about all that was allocated. It costs very little.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_stacks=This Java has no Flight Recorder (Java 16 or later is needed). The scanned thread's stack was sampled instead, with the bytes it allocated in between: who allocates is known roughly, what type of objects is not.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_share=Share
Of all the bytes allocated in the threads shown.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_bytes=Allocated
The bytes of the objects created over the whole scan (as the samples add up).
lagfinder.tip.alloc_rate=A second
The same, a second on average: how hard the line works the garbage collector.
lagfinder.tip.alloc_trend=Over time
How much was allocated along the scan: a steady rate, or bursts.
